// Repair a store written before integers were cut to the machine's thirty
// bits (frames/README.md, "An integer is thirty bits, however wide the
// host's word is").
//
// While the host's integers could be wider than the Newton's, an alarm
// went into the SystemAlarmSoup with an index key that narrowed the moment
// it was written, so the index holds a key no entry has.  The alarm can
// never be removed again, and because AddAlarm removes the alarm it
// replaces, every boot from then on fails to set the To Do list's
// roll-over alarm - which that application reports as
//
//     "There is not enough space in the internal memory to automatically
//      roll-over To Do tasks.  Deleting some data and resetting may help."
//
// Nothing is wrong with the memory, and nothing else in the store is
// affected: it is only the alarm soup's indexes.  This drops that soup,
// which the ROM builds again the next time an alarm is set.  Alarms
// already set are lost, which on a machine that cannot set one is no loss.
//
//   build/host/host/newton --rom build/MP2x00US/rom.bin --headless 5 \
//       --store build/newton.store --script src/host/demo/repair-alarms.ns
//
// Then start the machine as usual; the message should be gone.

begin
	local soup := GetStores()[0]:GetSoup("SystemAlarmSoup");
	if soup then
		begin
			soup:RemoveFromStore();
			Print("repair-alarms: the alarm soup is gone; the ROM will make a new one");
			Print("repair-alarms: the Query exceptions after this are the alarm code");
			Print("repair-alarms: finding the soup it was holding gone - the next boot is clean");
		end
	else
		Print("repair-alarms: there is no alarm soup - nothing to repair");
end;
